WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.131
Scene reading begins with orientation.

00:00:02.131 --> 00:00:06.194
Identify image direction, scale, date, time, sensor, and location confidence.

00:00:06.194 --> 00:00:09.850
Locate stable reference features before examining change or movement.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:15.131
Without orientation, a plausible interpretation may belong to the wrong place or direction.

00:00:15.131 --> 00:00:19.600
Visible features may include roads, paths, buildings, vehicles, terrain, vegetation, water,

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.631
construction, access routes, and hazards.

00:00:21.631 --> 00:00:23.662
Describe shape, position, count, condition,

00:00:23.662 --> 00:00:26.912
and relationship using neutral language before assigning meaning.

00:00:26.912 --> 00:00:30.975
Movement patterns can be observed in video or repeated frames,

00:00:30.975 --> 00:00:33.006
but they rarely establish motive.

00:00:33.006 --> 00:00:37.881
A stopped vehicle, gathered people, or changed route may have many explanations.

00:00:37.881 --> 00:00:40.724
Report the visible behavior and preserve alternatives.

00:00:40.724 --> 00:00:44.381
Shadows, roofs, trees, terrain, and perspective can hide features.

00:00:44.381 --> 00:00:48.849
Distance can compress space, while oblique angles can make objects overlap.

00:00:48.849 --> 00:00:54.130
Seasonal vegetation and temporary materials can change appearance without indicating a meaningful event.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:55.755
Separate observation from interpretation.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:01:00.630
An observation might be that water covers a marked section of road.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:04.287
An interpretation may be that the route is impassable.

00:01:04.287 --> 00:01:07.536
The second judgment may require depth, vehicle, ground,

00:01:07.536 --> 00:01:10.786
or official information not visible in the image.

00:01:10.786 --> 00:01:13.224
Use annotations and evidence references carefully.

00:01:13.224 --> 00:01:17.693
Mark the exact source frame and location, avoid covering important pixels,

00:01:17.693 --> 00:01:20.536
and distinguish confirmed features from tentative identifications.

00:01:20.536 --> 00:01:23.380
Honest limits make the observation more useful.
